+## Deactivate a location
+
+Open **Settings → Locations**, choose the location and switch **Active** off,
+then save. NEVORA asks **Deactivate {location}?** and explains: "The Clocker link
+will stop working here. Past schedules and time records will stay available."
+Choose **Deactivate** to continue or **Keep active** to leave it as it is.
+
+If work at the location is still open, the save stops with **{location} can’t be
+deactivated yet** and lists what to review. Each link opens in a new tab, so your
+edits stay on the form:
+
+- **Reassign or cancel shifts, then publish changes**: ongoing or future shifts,
+  draft or published, are still scheduled there.
+- **Review posted open shifts**: unclaimed open shifts there are still posted;
+  withdraw the ones you no longer need.
+- **Review open time in Timecards**: someone is still clocked in there; close the
+  open punch with the verified time.
+- **Review pending time corrections**: decide the time corrections waiting for
+  that location.
+- **Review pending shift requests**: decide the can't-work, swap or cover
+  requests waiting on its shifts.
+
+Resolve each one, then save again. When it succeeds, the page says **{location}
+is inactive**: the Clocker link is unavailable, and past schedules and time
+records are kept. If the result can't be confirmed, choose **Check again** before
+trying a second time; your entries are kept.
+
+## Activity log
+
+Open **Settings → Activity log** to see recorded changes, newest first. Only
+Owners can open it. It lists published schedules and edits to a published
+schedule, schedule changes after a shift exchange or a can't-work request,
+Manager access assigned or removed, employees activated or deactivated, and wage
+changes. Each entry says who made the change (**Changed by**) and the week or
+locations it affected. Use **Older changes** and **Newer changes** to move
+through the log. It is a record of what changed, not an approval or a way to undo
+a change.
+
+## Delete your own account
+
+Open **Profile → Delete my account**. This deletes your NEVORA account, not the
+company. The page shows what happens before you confirm:
+
+- **What we delete**: "Your access ends right away: you’re signed out on every
+  device and can’t sign in again with your password or a passkey. Calendar feed
+  links and device alerts stop." and "Within 30 calendar days after we receive
+  the request, we aim to delete your profile, sign-in details, notification
+  subscriptions, calendar links and the content you contributed. After you
+  confirm, you can’t cancel it in the app."
+- **What {company} keeps**: "Deleting your NEVORA account doesn’t end your
+  employment or remove records your employer has to keep." and "Your company’s
+  workspace stays open for the rest of your team. To close it, email
+  support@thevelani.com." **What may be kept** opens the retention details.
+
+To confirm, enter your password, check **I understand my NEVORA account will be
+deleted and I won’t be able to sign in again.** and choose **Delete my account**.
+**This can’t be undone.** NEVORA then signs you out everywhere and shows your
+reference; keep it until the deletion is done.
+
+If you're the only Owner, nothing is deleted: the page says **You’re the only
+Owner** because a workplace needs at least one Owner who can sign in. Add another
+Owner first (**Go to Team**), wait until they can sign in, then confirm again.
+Closing the company is a separate request: "Email support and we will walk you
+through it. Writing to us does not close the company or cancel billing by
+itself."
